58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/recruiting/story/_/id/38895893/how-top-50-2023-recruits-done-college-freshmen","type":"Story","byline":"Blake Baumgartner and Tom VanHaaren","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen flips again, now off to Oklahoma","description":"Five-star safety prospect Peyton Bowen, who previously flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon, has flipped once again, signing with Oklahoma Sooners, he announced on Twitter on Thursday.","published":"2024-01-23T16:02:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/35306416/five-star-safety-peyton-bowen-flips-again-now-oklahoma","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Blake Baumgartner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen flips from Notre Dame to Oregon","description":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen, the No. 14 overall prospect in the 2023 ESPN 300, has flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon on national signing day.","published":"2024-01-15T20:32:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/35298055/five-star-safety-peyton-bowen-flips-notre-dame-oregon","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Blake Baumgartner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"BYU retains CFP hopes, beats Kansas in triple overtime","description":"Bear Bachmeier connected with Jojo Phillips in the back of the end zone in the third overtime, helping No. 10 BYU beat Kansas to keep its CFP hopes alive.","published":"2026-11-21T21:39:12.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50553754/byu-retains-cfp-hopes-beats-kansas-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska snaps AP Top 25 losing skid, upsets Ohio State","description":"Nebraska broke its 31-game losing streak against AP Top 25 opponents with a 31-28 victory over No. 16 Ohio State on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-21T21:11:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50553426/nebraska-snaps-ap-top-25-losing-skid-upsets-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's Matt Rhule ends his drought against ranked opponents","description":"Rhule and Nebraska brought an end to the Cornhuskers coach's infamous decade-long streak against Ohio State.","published":"2026-11-21T20:58:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534102/nebraska-cornhuskers-matt-rhule-ranked-win-drought","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse QB Steve Angeli exits with injury, arm in sling","description":"Syracuse senior quarterback Steve Angeli left Saturday's game against Boston College with an injury to his throwing arm and will not return.","published":"2026-11-21T20:51:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50552810/syracuse-qb-steve-angeli-exits-injury-arm-sling","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-21T18:35:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Army pulls seating prank at Navy's football stadium ahead of Memphis game","description":"The letters were adjusted back in time for Navy's kickoff.","published":"2026-11-21T18:47:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50551457/army-navy-seat-prank","type":"Story","byline":"Associated Press","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Keisean Henderson leads Houston to win after QB Conner Weigman ruled out","description":"Houston ruled out starting QB Conner Weigman vs. West Virginia due to injury and instead went with true freshman Keisean Henderson, the No. 4 recruit for 2026.","published":"2026-11-21T21:38:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50550966/sources-houston-qb-conner-weigman-henderson-start","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870625/peyton-bowen","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peyton_Bowen"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Peyton Bowen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peyton_Bowen","description":"American football cornerback (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:34:50Z","intro":"Peyton Bowen (born March 1, 2004) is an American college football safety for the Oklahoma Sooners.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Bowen grew up in Denton, Texas. He attended and played high school football at John H. Guyer High School. He intercepted 12 passes and broke up 23 passes in three varsity seasons at Guyer.\n\nRECRUITMENT\nBowen was rated a five-star recruit by ESPN and initially committed Notre Dame over offers from Alabama, Oklahoma, and USC. He later flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon. However, the following day Bowen changed his commitment a second time and signed his National Letter of Intent to play at Oklahoma. He later explained that his decision was due to a paperwork issue as Oregon had not sent him a letter of intent to sign before the start of the early signing period."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Bowen joined the Oklahoma Sooners as an early enrollee in January 2023. He entered the season as the team's second-string safety."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Eli Bowen","description":"American football player","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_Bowen_(American_football)"}]}}